# CLAUDE.md — app/Enums

Enums are the domain vocabulary: string-backed, TitleCase cases. Codes and display labels live HERE (`label()`,
per-case predicates), never duplicated in controllers, resources or views.

Lifecycle enums (any status column) own the state machine: `canTransitionTo()`, `allowedTransitions()`,
terminal-state predicates, and **a named predicate per domain question** instead of status lists at call sites
(`app/Models/CLAUDE.md`, state discipline).

<!-- if:htmx -->
Blade renders `$model->status->label()`, never a `match` on `->value`. A per-case colour or icon is a method here
(`badgeClass()`), so the mapping exists once.

<!-- endif -->
Outcome enums (a job's result, a sync's status) carry an explicit `Unreachable` / `Failed` case, distinct from
"nothing happened".

**Never enumerate secrets or external identifiers** (API model names, vendor account ids) as cases; they live in
config.
<!-- house:end -->
